Subject: [PATCH v1 0/2] Look up provision.db in the configured data directory
To: ofono@lists.linux.dev

provision_db_new_default() hard-codes /usr/share/ofono/provision.db,
but the database is installed into $(pkgdatadir). With any prefix other
than /usr automatic provisioning fails with "Unable to open provisioning
database!". Patch 1 passes pkgdatadir to the sources, patch 2 uses it.

Tested by building 2.19 with both patches on NixOS: ofonod now
references $prefix/share/ofono/provision.db, and on a Fairphone 6
(NixOS) an equivalent path fix makes the internet context get
provisioned automatically.

Development was assisted by an AI coding tool (see the Co-Authored-By
trailer).

Paul Schuldesz (2):
  build: Pass pkgdatadir to the sources as PKGDATADIR
  provisiondb: Look up the default database in PKGDATADIR

 Makefile.am       | 1 +
 src/provisiondb.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

